      "record_kind": "published",
      "notes": "This is the ruby-pressure assignment of the same 16-row compression/decompression experiment represented by the companion ice-VII-scale record. It is a distinct fit, not a duplicate parameter transcription. The paper reports that V0 was varied and stayed within 0.01% of the measured in-cell value, while K0 was fixed at the adopted 212 GPa Brillouin value. Ruby-line broadening above 15 GPa showed increasing nonhydrostatic stress; the authors therefore regarded K0'=7.5 as less realistic than the ice-VII-scale result. The source gives neither parameter covariance nor a confidence convention for parenthesized fit errors, and it does not specify an exact ruby calibration equation. The numerical 298 K reference encodes the source's qualitative 'ambient temperature' wording rather than a measured sample temperature.",
